# 05 — Spec Documents

## Where Specs Go

Write working specs, execution plans, design proposals, and debugging notes as markdown files in the `.spec` directory.

## Filename Date Prefix

Start each new spec filename with the local calendar date on which you create the file, written `YYYY-MM-DD-` (example: `2026-11-04-ferry-playback-execution-plan.md`).

Never change that prefix later. Keep it when the file is edited, committed, or moved on a later day. A filename that already starts with `YYYY-MM-DD-` keeps its existing prefix.

## Completed Specs

When a spec moves to `.spec/completed/`, it keeps its prefix and goes in the month directory `YYYY-MM` taken from that prefix (example: `.spec/completed/2026-11/2026-11-04-ferry-playback-execution-plan.md`).

## Living Documentation

Living product documentation belongs in `doc/`, not `.spec`. This includes the UX specification suite (`doc/ux-specification.md` and the `doc/ux/` folder) and the mechanics documents indexed by `doc/README.md`. Update those documents in place; do not copy them into `.spec`.
